  "provenance": "Creality Ender-3 V3 / V3 Plus (CoreXZ) toolhead (unicorn quick-swap nozzle, ceramic heater, front cover with side duct outlets) Confidence: low. Sources: https://www.printables.com/model/1140984 (EBD Design Studio, Ender-3 V3/V3 Plus toolhead cover, remixed to match the stock cover; STL used for the cover shape); https://www.printables.com/model/1269694 (stock cover has duct outlets on the sides); https://www.printables.com/model/1339374 (remix of the stock Ender-3 V3 CoreXZ toolhead; same 49.7 x 57.8 x 98.5 mm cover envelope); Hotend heights taken from the K2-series unicorn hotend CAD https://www.printables.com/model/1415219. No CAD of the stock Ender-3 V3 hotend/carriage found. The cover shape is a community remix matching the stock cover (49.7 x 57.8 x 98.5 mm, identical envelope in a second remix); placed with the nozzle at the centre of the U-arch that wraps the heater (STL x=110, y=105.8), rotated 180 deg so the arch opening faces +Y (carriage side). Vertical datum estimated: the Ender-3 V3 uses the K2/K1C-family unicorn nozzle + ceramic heater, whose sock bottom is 4.0 mm above the tip (K2 CAD) and whose cover edge sits at 4.1 mm; cover lowest edge here is set to 3.5 mm (0.5 mm lower for uncertainty). Gantry z and carriage box are estimates (head mounts to the X carriage on the back; no gantry CAD). Same toolhead on the Ender-3 V3 Plus. Nozzle: land radius 0.40 mm, 38.1-degree cone to Z=2.60, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 30.00 mm above the tip, Y 17.0..55.0, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/creality-ender3-v3.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
